add('data-erasure-services-india', 'Data Erasure & Data Wiping Services India | e2e',
    'Data erasure and sanitization for corporate laptops, HDDs, SSDs and servers. Blancco, TruWipe and BitRaser workflows, reporting and Pan-India collection.',
    'Data erasure and sanitization services for corporate IT teams',
    'Retire, redeploy or return company equipment with a planned data wiping process. e2e provides data sanitization for corporate laptops, desktops, workstations, servers and loose storage drives, alongside Pan-India collection and recycling when required.',
    section('Wiping is a service in its own right', '<p>You can enquire about erasure while retaining ownership of your equipment. Tell us whether assets will return to employees, move to another office, leave on a lease return, or enter a recycling program. Agree the release criteria before any device changes hands.</p><p>For an office refresh, separate usable laptops from failed drives and non-storage equipment. A monitor collection and a server drive wiping project need different handling, pricing and evidence.</p>') +
    section('Blancco, TruWipe and BitRaser data wiping workflows', '<p>e2e uses erasure tools including Blancco, TruWipe and BitRaser. Specify your required software, drive models and reporting format in your enquiry. The selected product, version, licences, supported media and method are confirmed in the proposal.</p><p>For vendor capabilities, see ' + BLANCCO + ', ' + TRUWIPE + ' and ' + BITRASER + '. Review the proposed product and its reporting against your requirements during procurement.</p>') +
    section('Choose the route for each storage device', table(['Asset', 'Information to share', 'Decision before release'], [
        ['Laptop or workstation', 'Model, drive type, quantity, encryption and reuse plan', 'Confirm access, supported method and device-level reporting'],
        ['HDD, SSD or NVMe drive', 'Model, serial number, interface and health', 'Assess media compatibility; isolate unsuccessful erasures'],
        ['Server or storage array', 'Drive count, controllers, RAID and maintenance window', 'Map individual media to the system inventory'],
        ['Failed or inaccessible drive', 'Fault details and security classification', 'Agree physical destruction if erasure cannot be validated']])) +
    section('Agree the evidence before the job', '<p>Define the asset identifiers, chosen technique, result, exceptions, date and acceptance owner needed for your records. Request a sample reporting format during procurement. Keep unsuccessful drives under control until your IT owner approves their next step.</p><p>' + NIST + ' is a reference for planning a sanitization program. Your security policy, media characteristics and agreed acceptance criteria determine the actual scope. NIST does not certify e2e or an individual wiping job.</p>') +
    section('Tell us what your IT team needs', bullets(['Site city and number of data-bearing devices or loose drives.', 'Whether equipment can leave the premises; request an onsite feasibility assessment if it cannot.', 'Approved erasure software, reporting format and retention requirements.', 'Reuse, return or recycling decision, and handling of failed media.']) + '<p>' + link('it-disposal-brief.html', 'Build a data erasure enquiry brief') + ' or email the scope to info@e2erecycling.com. Onsite execution, access arrangements, turnaround and fees are agreed after assessment.</p>'),
    [('Can we book data wiping without recycling the equipment?', 'Yes. Enquire about data erasure for equipment you intend to retain, redeploy or return. e2e will confirm supported media, handling arrangements, reporting and scope before work.'),
     ('Do you use Blancco, TruWipe and BitRaser?', 'e2e uses tools including Blancco, TruWipe and BitRaser. Specify your required tool, media and report format; the exact product and workflow are agreed in the proposal.'),
     ('What happens if a drive cannot be erased?', 'A failed or unsupported drive must be recorded as an exception. Agree a controlled alternative such as physical drive destruction before releasing it.'),
     ('Can you wipe drives at our office?', 'Request an onsite feasibility assessment. Execution depends on the city, site access, power, workspace, drive compatibility, security requirements and agreed scope.')], related=['data-erasure-vs-drive-destruction', 'data-erasure-certificate-checklist', 'hard-drive-destruction-services', 'locations'])

add('corporate-it-asset-disposal', 'Corporate IT Asset Disposal & E-Waste Recycling India | e2e',
    'Dispose of company laptops, desktops, monitors, workstations and electronics with e2e. KSPCB-registered recycling, data sanitization and Pan-India collection.',
    'Corporate IT asset disposal and office electronics recycling',
    'e2e helps IT departments and facilities teams dispose of retired office equipment through assessment, collection, data sanitization and recycling. We are a KSPCB-registered recycler with Pan-India collection and logistics.',
    section('One plan for an office refresh or clearance', '<p>Old computers often accumulate across storage rooms, branch offices and IT support desks. Start with an asset list and an owner for release approval. We help scope a one-time clearance or recurring collection program around the mix of equipment, data exposure and site constraints.</p>' + table(['Equipment', 'Before handover'], [['Company laptops and desktops', 'Record asset tags and storage devices; approve erasure or destruction.'], ['Engineering workstations', 'Identify every installed drive and decide which components are retained.'], ['Monitors and displays', 'Record quantity, condition and packing needs; flag damaged screens.'], ['Servers and network equipment', 'Confirm decommissioning, embedded storage and configuration handling.'], ['Office electronics and accessories', 'List printers, cables and peripherals separately; identify items with internal storage.']])) +
    section('Collection, logistics and reporting', '<p>Share pickup addresses, floor access, loading restrictions, contact persons and approximate quantities. We confirm the collection scope and schedule before dispatch. Multi-office jobs should use one inventory format with a separate site code for each location.</p><p>At handover, reconcile the equipment released with the agreed collection record. Decide which data-bearing devices remain onsite pending security approval. Arrange the required recycling and data-handling records as part of the service scope.</p>') +
    section('Data protection comes before disposal', '<p>Do not treat an operating-system reset or a removed user account as proof of sanitization. Agree a storage-specific erasure workflow or physical destruction route for each data-bearing asset. Keep backups and release approvals with your internal IT team.</p><p>Our ' + link('data-erasure-services-india.html', 'corporate data erasure service') + ' can be scoped separately for equipment that will be reused or returned.</p>') +
    section('Vendor checks for procurement teams', '<p>Ask for current registration documents, their scope and validity, the processing route, a sample collection record and the agreed reporting package. State your company requirements in the purchase order. Registration evidence and project records should be reviewed together.</p><p>Use the ' + CPCB + ' to review current official information. e2e’s stated registration is with KSPCB; request documents for your vendor review rather than assuming any additional certification.</p>') +
    section('Prepare a useful quote request', bullets(['Count laptops, desktops, monitors, servers and accessories separately.', 'Identify storage media, preferred sanitization and any onsite-only restrictions.', 'List all cities and collection sites, with target windows and site access.', 'Specify records needed by IT, finance, procurement and facilities.']) + '<p>' + link('it-disposal-brief.html', 'Create your corporate disposal brief') + ' and attach your inventory to the email. Pricing depends on scope, condition, location, logistics and data-handling work.</p>'),
    [('Do you collect old company laptops and monitors?', 'Yes. e2e scopes corporate collections for laptops, desktops, monitors, workstations, servers and office electronics. Share quantities, locations, data requirements and access details.'),
     ('Is collection available across India?', 'e2e provides Pan-India collection and logistics. Each site, asset mix and pickup window is confirmed during assessment.'),
     ('Do you offer free pickup or a fixed scrap price?', 'Collection fees and any recoverable asset value depend on equipment, volume, condition, location and data work. Request a scoped quotation rather than assuming free pickup or a fixed value.')], related=['data-erasure-services-india', 'server-recycling-india', 'corporate-laptop-disposal-checklist', 'locations'])

add('server-recycling-india', 'Server Recycling & Workstation Disposal India | e2e',
    'Plan corporate server recycling, workstation disposal and storage media sanitization. e2e coordinates assessment, collection and recycling across India.',
    'Server recycling, storage retirement and workstation disposal',
    'Plan the retirement of company servers, engineering workstations and storage equipment with e2e. Our recycling and data sanitization services help IT teams turn an approved decommissioning plan into an organised collection and disposal project.',
    section('Define what is ready to leave service', '<p>Your IT team owns production shutdown, migration, backup validation and approval to retire equipment. Once that approval is in place, e2e can assess the physical assets, storage media, collection arrangements and recycling requirements. Identify any devices still under lease, warranty return, legal hold or internal retention.</p><p>List chassis and media separately: a server with multiple disks needs a clearer inventory than a single asset-tag entry. Include storage shelves, loose drives, controllers and any removable modules that can hold data.</p>') +
    section('Storage decisions need a media inventory', bullets(['Map each drive serial number to its parent server or workstation.', 'Identify HDD, SSD, NVMe and other media rather than requesting one method for everything.', 'State whether drives may leave the site before sanitization.', 'Set an exception route for failed disks, locked devices and inaccessible storage.', 'Agree the final report structure and who signs off reconciliation.'])) +
    section('Coordinate the physical handover', '<p>For equipment in server rooms or controlled facilities, specify access approvals, loading routes, packing requirements and the collection window. Confirm whether racks, rails and accessories are included. De-racking, electrical isolation and production changes must be assigned explicitly rather than assumed as part of a recycling collection.</p><p>For distributed sites, separate the project into approved batches. Record what was collected, what remained onsite and why. This allows your IT owner to close inventory exceptions before final disposal approval.</p>') +
    section('Connect recycling and sanitization', '<p>Working media intended for reuse can be assessed for ' + link('data-erasure-services-india.html', 'software-based data erasure') + '. Failed media or media your policy requires to be destroyed can follow an agreed ' + link('hard-drive-destruction-services.html', 'physical drive destruction route') + '. The equipment and its data do not need to follow the same outcome.</p><p>e2e offers Pan-India collection; site logistics, any onsite work and reporting are confirmed after assessment. Share equipment lists and drive counts before requesting a collection date.</p>'),
    [('Can you recycle servers with drives still installed?', 'Include every storage device in the inventory and agree its sanitization or destruction route before collection. e2e will assess handling and reporting requirements for the complete scope.'),
     ('Do you shut down or migrate our production servers?', 'Production shutdown, migration, backups and release approvals remain with your authorised IT team. Any additional physical work must be specified and agreed separately.')], related=['server-decommissioning-checklist', 'data-erasure-certificate-checklist', 'corporate-it-asset-disposal', 'locations'])

add('hard-drive-destruction-services', 'Hard Drive Destruction Services India | e2e Recycling',
    'Physical drive destruction for corporate HDDs, SSDs and failed storage media. Plan asset records, handling and recycling with e2e across India.',
    'Physical hard drive and storage media destruction for businesses',
    'e2e provides physical drive destruction for corporate storage media that must not return to use. Scope the equipment, handling, identification and evidence your IT security team needs before approving collection or processing.',
    section('When destruction belongs in the plan', '<p>Physical destruction is an option when a drive has failed, a supported erasure route is unavailable, or your internal policy requires the media to be destroyed. Decide this before assets leave controlled storage. A failed software operation should remain an open exception until a responsible person approves the next action.</p><p>Destruction and erasure have different commercial outcomes: physical destruction prevents reuse of the media. For working equipment your team wants to retain, consider a separate ' + link('data-erasure-services-india.html', 'data wiping assessment') + '.</p>') +
    section('HDDs and SSDs require a defined scope', '<p>Identify the media type, model, condition and quantity. SSDs store data in flash components, while HDDs use magnetic media; a method described only as “drive destruction” does not tell procurement what will actually happen. Agree a suitable physical process, acceptance criteria and the evidence available for your specific media.</p><p>Ask about the location of processing, whether witnessing is required and feasible, how items are tracked, and how resulting material enters the recycling route. Any onsite execution or witnessing arrangement is confirmed in the proposal.</p>') +
    section('Records to request', bullets(['Approved media list, with serial numbers or agreed identifiers.', 'Collection and transfer records covering the custody handovers.', 'Agreed destruction method and processing location.', 'Completion evidence tied to the media list, with discrepancies recorded.', 'Recycling records for the resulting material where included in scope.'])) +
    section('Prototype and confidential equipment destruction', '<p>e2e also handles prototype destruction. Describe the material, dimensions, quantity and confidentiality controls. Identify storage devices inside prototypes so that intellectual-property handling and data security are both addressed.</p><p>' + link('it-disposal-brief.html', 'Prepare a destruction enquiry') + ' with the city, media quantities, security requirements and your preferred completion window. Do not send passwords or the contents of the drives.</p>'),
    [('Is drive destruction the same as data erasure?', 'No. Erasure aims to sanitize compatible media while allowing reuse. Physical destruction makes the media unusable. Choose the route according to your policy, media condition and acceptance criteria.'),
     ('Can failed SSDs and HDDs be included?', 'Yes, include failed media in your enquiry. e2e will assess media types, the destruction process and required records before confirming the job.')], related=['data-erasure-vs-drive-destruction', 'data-erasure-services-india', 'server-recycling-india'])

