add('locations', 'Corporate E-Waste Collection Across Indian Cities | e2e',
    'Pan-India corporate e-waste collection and data erasure enquiries: Bengaluru, Chennai, Hyderabad, Mumbai, Pune, Delhi NCR, Kolkata, Ahmedabad and more.',
    'Pan-India corporate e-waste collection and data erasure coverage',
    'e2e coordinates collection and logistics across India for corporate IT equipment and electronic waste. Bengaluru, Chennai and Hyderabad are priority service markets; other metropolitan and branch-office collections are scoped through our national service.',
    section('Metropolitan collection planning', '<p>Use this coverage guide to prepare an enquiry for one office or a national refresh. These are service areas, not claimed branch addresses. Collection feasibility, transport, execution location and completion dates are confirmed against your actual sites.</p>'+table(['City / region','Coverage guide','Planning detail'],metro_rows)) +
    section('One asset register, separate site records', '<p>National projects work best when IT and procurement use one asset template, with a unique site code per pickup. Identify counts, data-bearing devices, local contacts, access hours and a release owner for each office. Flag any interstate movement or internal documentation requirements for the logistics review.</p><p>Keep collection, sanitization and recycling completion as separate milestones. A truck leaving an office does not mean that data work is complete. Reconcile the final outcome against each site inventory.</p>') +
    section('Data work across multiple offices', '<p>Tell us whether drives must remain onsite until sanitization, can move under agreed custody arrangements, or must be physically destroyed. Different sites may have different restrictions. e2e will review onsite feasibility and the reporting plan before confirming execution.</p><p>'+link('data-erasure-services-india.html','Explore data erasure services')+' or use the '+link('multi-office-e-waste-collection-plan.html','multi-office collection guide')+' to prepare an internal scope.</p>'),
    [('Do you have a branch in every city listed?', 'No. e2e is based in Tumkur, Karnataka. The city list describes Pan-India collection coverage and project enquiries, not a network of claimed local offices.'),
     ('Can one enquiry cover several Indian offices?', 'Yes. Provide a site-by-site inventory, addresses, local contacts, data-handling requirements and collection windows. e2e will assess a coordinated scope and reporting plan.')], kind='collection', related=['it-disposal-brief','corporate-it-asset-disposal','data-erasure-services-india'])

add('data-erasure-vs-drive-destruction', 'Data Erasure vs Drive Destruction: IT Buyer Guide | e2e',
    'Compare data wiping, sanitization and physical drive destruction for company laptops, HDDs, SSDs and servers. A practical decision guide for IT buyers.',
    'Data erasure or physical drive destruction: which should IT choose?',
    'Choose based on the media, its condition, your security policy and whether it will be reused. Erasure can preserve compatible working media; physical destruction removes that reuse option. Both routes need an agreed result and records.',
    section('Start with the outcome', table(['Question','Erasure route','Destruction route'],[['Will the drive return to use?','Assess a compatible erasure method and acceptance checks.','The media will not be reusable.'],['Is the drive accessible and supported?','Confirm access, tool support and successful completion.','Consider when erasure is unavailable or fails.'],['Does policy mandate destruction?','Do not substitute wiping without approval.','Define a media-appropriate physical method.'],['What must the record show?','Media ID, method, result and exceptions.','Media ID, process completion and reconciliation.']])) +
    section('A wipe command is only part of the work', '<p>First authorise the retirement and confirm that required data has been retained. Then identify every storage device, choose the treatment and define who accepts the outcome. This prevents a successful operation on one disk from being mistaken for clearance of an entire multi-drive system.</p><p>For SSDs and NVMe media, confirm the model and supported workflow rather than relying on an HDD overwrite assumption. Failed or inaccessible media needs its own approved route.</p>') +
    section('Use a simple decision sequence', '<ol><li>Record the equipment and media identifiers.</li><li>Confirm policy and intended reuse, return or recycling.</li><li>Assess media condition and compatibility.</li><li>Agree the method, evidence and failure route.</li><li>Reconcile results before releasing equipment.</li></ol><p>'+NIST+' provides current program guidance. Method selection and acceptance remain specific to the media and your organisation.</p>') +
    section('Buy the service your project needs', '<p>Ask for '+link('data-erasure-services-india.html','data erasure')+' when retaining equipment is part of the plan. Ask for '+link('hard-drive-destruction-services.html','physical drive destruction')+' when the media must not return to use. A mixed fleet can need both, with separate outcomes recorded against the same asset register.</p>'),
    [('Does deleting files count as a documented erasure service?', 'Deleting files or reinstalling an operating system alone does not establish an accepted sanitization outcome. Define the media treatment, checks and evidence with your IT security owner.')], kind='article', related=['data-erasure-certificate-checklist','data-erasure-services-india'])

add('corporate-laptop-disposal-checklist', 'Corporate Laptop Disposal Checklist for IT Teams | e2e',
    'A practical company laptop retirement checklist: approvals, asset inventory, backups, data wiping, collection records and recycling handover.',
    'Corporate laptop disposal checklist for IT and procurement',
    'Before disposing of company laptops, approve the retirement, reconcile devices and drives, retain required data, agree sanitization and record the final handover. Use this checklist for a refresh, lease return or office clearance.',
    section('1. Establish ownership and release approval', '<p>Reconcile your asset register with the physical stock. Include devices held by remote employees, support teams and storage rooms. Check ownership, lease conditions and any retention hold. Nominate the person who can authorise each device to leave the company.</p>') +
    section('2. Prepare the data and device inventory', bullets(['Confirm backups and retention with the data owner before any erasure.', 'Record asset tag, manufacturer, model, serial number and installed drive details.', 'Note damaged devices, missing drives and systems that will not power on.', 'Remove access locks and management assignments only through your approved IT process.', 'Keep passwords and customer data out of the collection spreadsheet.'])) +
    section('3. Separate the intended outcomes', '<p>Group equipment by redeployment, lease return, reuse assessment or recycling. Select '+link('data-erasure-services-india.html','data wiping')+' or '+link('hard-drive-destruction-services.html','media destruction')+' according to your policy and the condition of each drive. Agree how unsuccessful operations will be reported and held.</p><p>Do not promise release of a whole batch until exceptions have an owner. A laptop chassis and its storage media may require separate decisions.</p>') +
    section('4. Prepare collection with facilities', '<p>Set pickup addresses, access hours, loading arrangements, packing responsibilities and onsite contacts. Label batches so the collection team can distinguish cleared equipment from stock still awaiting approval. Count monitors, docking stations, chargers and accessories separately.</p>') +
    section('5. Close the records', '<p>Match the handover list to the collection record and reconcile data-handling outcomes against media identifiers. Record what was not collected, what could not be processed and what needs follow-up. File the agreed recycling and sanitization records alongside the retirement approval.</p><p>'+link('assets/downloads/corporate-it-asset-inventory.csv','Download the blank asset inventory CSV')+' or '+link('it-disposal-brief.html','prepare a collection brief')+'. The template is a planning aid; adapt its fields to your internal controls.</p>'),
    [('Should our IT team wipe laptops before collection?', 'Follow your internal data policy. If third-party erasure is required, agree whether media can leave the premises, the processing location, method and records before collection.')],kind='article',related=['corporate-it-asset-disposal','data-erasure-certificate-checklist','locations'])

add('server-decommissioning-checklist', 'Server Decommissioning & Disposal Checklist | e2e',
    'Plan server retirement after shutdown approval: drive mapping, sanitization, exception handling, equipment collection and recycling records.',
    'Server decommissioning checklist before recycling or disposal',
    'Complete your internal shutdown and release approvals before arranging server disposal. Then inventory every storage device, agree data handling, plan physical access and reconcile the final equipment and media outcomes.',
    section('Keep production changes with the authorised team', '<p>Migration, application dependencies, backup testing and shutdown approval belong in your IT change process. A recycling collection should begin with assets already approved for retirement. Confirm any lease, return, retention or security restrictions before scheduling physical movement.</p>') +
    section('Create a chassis-to-media register', '<p>Record the server asset tag and chassis serial number, then list the drives beneath it. Include storage shelves, hot spares, loose disks and removed components. Record interfaces, capacities and health where known. Do not assume that all disks share one condition or one approved treatment.</p><p>For arrays or RAID controllers, confirm how individual media will be accessible for the agreed process. This is a compatibility question to resolve before the job, not after equipment arrives for processing.</p>') +
    section('Agree treatment and exceptions', bullets(['State whether media can leave the premises before sanitization.', 'Select the reuse or destruction outcome with your security owner.', 'Request an appropriate erasure workflow for each supported media type.', 'Assign failed, inaccessible or unidentified media a controlled exception route.', 'Define final acceptance and reconciliation responsibilities.'])) +
    section('Prepare the physical collection', '<p>Specify equipment location, access controls, loading route, packing, rack rails and accessories. Assign de-racking and isolation work explicitly if required. Separate the collection window from the sanitization completion target, and allow for exceptions in the project plan.</p><p>After collection, match chassis and media records to their outcomes. Resolve missing identifiers before closing the disposal project.</p>') +
    section('Get an equipment retirement scope', '<p>e2e can assess '+link('server-recycling-india.html','server recycling and workstation disposal')+' alongside '+link('data-erasure-services-india.html','data sanitization')+'. Send a device list, drive counts, cities and your required evidence. The '+link('assets/downloads/corporate-it-asset-inventory.csv','asset inventory template')+' includes a parent asset field for media mapping.</p>'),
    [('Does one server asset tag cover all drive records?', 'A chassis asset tag is useful, but a multi-drive server needs media-level mapping when individual sanitization or destruction outcomes must be reconciled.')],kind='article',related=['server-recycling-india','data-erasure-certificate-checklist','data-erasure-vs-drive-destruction'])

add('data-erasure-certificate-checklist', 'Data Erasure Certificate & Report Checklist | e2e',
    'What should IT buyers check in a data erasure report? Review media identifiers, methods, results, exceptions and inventory reconciliation before acceptance.',
    'What to check in a data erasure certificate and report',
    'A useful erasure record lets your IT team trace the reported outcome to the exact storage device and retirement approval. Ask for a sample format before buying the service, then agree the fields and exceptions your team must review.',
    section('Review these fields before acceptance', table(['Field','Why your team needs it'],[['Asset and media identifiers','Connect a drive result to the equipment register.'],['Tool, version and selected method','Understand the workflow actually used.'],['Processing date and result','Distinguish completed treatment from pending work.'],['Verification and acceptance information','Understand checks and the decision to accept or reject the outcome.'],['Errors, exclusions and failed devices','Keep unresolved media visible.'],['Operator or accountable party and report reference','Provide a route for reconciliation and follow-up.']])) +
    section('Separate the different records', '<p>A pickup acknowledgement records a handover. An erasure report records a data treatment outcome. A destruction record describes a different process, while a recycling record addresses the equipment or material route. Agree which documents you need instead of accepting one generic certificate for every step.</p><p>'+BITRASER+' illustrates vendor report formats. The availability of an example does not establish what an individual e2e job includes; confirm the deliverables in the quotation.</p>') +
    section('Treat unsuccessful devices as exceptions', '<p>Keep failed, unsupported and unidentifiable media in an open list. Ask how the device is held, who approves a different method and which final record closes it. Reconcile counts as well as identifiers, including devices that were never presented for processing.</p><p>'+NIST+' distinguishes verification and validation within sanitization assurance. Your review process should identify who accepts the result.</p>') +
    section('Request the right scope from e2e', '<p>When enquiring about '+link('data-erasure-services-india.html','data erasure services')+', state your approved tool, required fields, reporting recipient and storage-media mix. Ask to review a sample report during procurement. Keep your actual records in your own controlled repository; never publish them as marketing material.</p>'),
    [('Does a certificate alone prove every asset was handled?', 'It must be reconciled against the agreed inventory and results. Review identifiers, completed outcomes and exceptions rather than relying on the certificate title alone.')],kind='article',related=['data-erasure-services-india','server-decommissioning-checklist','data-erasure-vs-drive-destruction'])

add('multi-office-e-waste-collection-plan', 'Multi-Office E-Waste Collection Plan for India | e2e',
    'Coordinate corporate e-waste collections across Indian offices with a site inventory, release owners, data-media rules and a common reporting plan.',
    'How to plan e-waste collection across multiple Indian offices',
    'Use one project scope with separate site inventories, release contacts and data-handling rules. This gives procurement a common view while allowing each office to confirm what is actually ready for collection.',
    section('Use one template with a site code', '<p>For each office, capture the city, full address, local contact, equipment counts, data-bearing media and preferred window. Use the same equipment categories so headquarters can compare quantities without reworking spreadsheets. Mark estimates as estimates until the local owner checks the physical stock.</p>') +
    section('Make security rules explicit at each site', '<p>One office may allow controlled transport of storage devices while another requires a review before any drive leaves. State those differences in the scope. If onsite work is needed, ask for a feasibility assessment rather than assuming identical delivery at every location.</p><p>Separate ordinary peripherals from systems with data storage. Identify prototypes and specialist electronics in their own list so confidential handling is planned.</p>') +
    section('Define milestones and responsibilities', bullets(['IT owner: authorises retirement, retention and media treatment.', 'Facilities contact: confirms access, packing arrangements and loading hours.', 'Procurement: confirms scope, documents, commercial terms and vendor checks.', 'Collection team: reconciles the agreed handover list.', 'Project owner: closes inventory and reporting exceptions after processing.'])) +
    section('Close sites individually', '<p>Track collection, sanitization, destruction and recycling as separate outcomes where applicable. Keep a list of equipment held back, quantities that changed and data work awaiting approval. Headquarters should be able to identify an unresolved item without reopening every office spreadsheet.</p><p>e2e provides '+link('locations.html','Pan-India collection and logistics')+'. Send one coordinated '+link('it-disposal-brief.html','project brief')+' with site details, and attach the '+link('assets/downloads/corporate-it-asset-inventory.csv','asset inventory')+' once your local owners have reconciled it.</p>'),
    [('Can a single quotation cover offices in different cities?', 'Request a coordinated scope with per-site quantities and requirements. Collection timing, logistics and any onsite work are assessed for each site before confirmation.')],kind='article',related=['locations','corporate-it-asset-disposal','corporate-laptop-disposal-checklist'])

